invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: ct.h takes CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL beside CH_CPU_RUNTIME, so the files under
  their own names, which every session without
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY runs, compile to the native multiply, and
  the bit picks between two copies of one multiply.
  test/widemul-builds.sh requires that build not to compile.

--- old
#if defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && defined(CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL)
#error "a host object takes the multiply's timing from ch_cfg.cpu: drop -DCH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL"
#endif
--- new
